# Shell scripts and systemd units run on Linux (the VPS). CRLF breaks them —
# a script with CRLF fails at exec with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M",
# and systemd silently mis-parses unit directives. Force LF regardless of platform.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.timer         text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
# Two gaps found 2026-08-08, both of which ship a broken file rather than fail a check.
# `Dockerfile` is an exact-name pattern, so deploy/db.Dockerfile matched nothing; and the
# operational scripts in deploy/ carry no .sh extension because they are installed onto PATH
# as commands (jobdigest-claude-verify, jobdigest-mem-sample), so *.sh missed them too. Both
# would have been checked out CRLF on Windows and shipped that way by `git archive`.
*.Dockerfile    text eol=lf
deploy/jobdigest-* text eol=lf
*.Caddyfile     text eol=lf
Caddyfile       text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
deploy/*.py     text eol=lf
